From c24f133d4d34d4a4629993b542c469f09a47aa1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Rutledge <shawn.rutledge@qt.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:13:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] QXcbClipboard::setMimeData: work with clipboard managers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tst_qquicktextedit::pasteHtmlIntoMarkdown was flaky, but that was just
a symptom of a race condition that could occur on any X11 desktop
running a clipboard manager implementing the ICCCM protocol: the moment
it sees the CLIPBOARD selection cleared, it races in with its own
SAVE_TARGETS selection-request (to grab/persist the outgoing content)
and then takes ownership itself, using a freshly fetched timestamp.
That sequence could land in the gap between clear() and copy():

- Clipman's SAVE_TARGETS request arrives after Qt already nulled
  m_clientClipboard[mode] in clear() → handleSelectionRequest() finds no
  data → "Cannot transfer data, no data available".

- Clipman grabs ownership with a newer timestamp than the test process's
  stale cached one.

If we then call xcb_set_selection_owner() with the older timestamp,
the X server rejects it per the ICCCM "ignore if time is not later than
current last-change-time" rule; so ownership never transfers back to
the test window, and selectionOwner(modeAtom) != newOwner, so we
emit the "Cannot set X11 selection owner" warning. The hasHtml() test
then reads whatever (or nothing) that clipman owns.

To fix this, get a new timestamp here.

Fixes: QTBUG-108346
Assisted-by: Claude Code Sonnet 5
Change-Id: I972b9c86e267841c5c5a1103bfb801eff5cde8ba
Reviewed-by: Axel Spoerl <axel.spoerl@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit ff130630d3d331b3cc80fe10bbf8d6a43ba781a8)
Reviewed-by: Qt Cherry-pick Bot <cherrypick_bot@qt-project.org>
Origin: upstream, https://invent.kde.org/qt/qt/qtbase/-/commit/c24f133d4d34d4a4629993b542c469f09a47aa1f
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-29
---
 src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp
index bf2a11c9423..9408bddc5b8 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbclipboard.cpp
@@ -323,8 +323,8 @@ void QXcbClipboard::setMimeData(QMimeData *data, QClipboard::Mode mode)
         m_timestamp[mode] = XCB_CURRENT_TIME;
     }
 
-    if (connection()->time() == XCB_CURRENT_TIME)
-        connection()->setTime(connection()->getTimestamp());
+    // fresh timestamp in case a clipboard manager takes over the selection with a newer time
+    connection()->setTime(connection()->getTimestamp());
 
     if (data) {
         newOwner = connection()->qtSelectionOwner();
